          "html_url": "https://github.com/bitcoin/bitcoin/commit/6b9903f39d0e19fd4898cb4ec621d5c15c573e87"
        }
      ],
      "message": "net: automatically mark IPv4/IPv6 as unreachable if there is no route\n\nCheck one minute after startup, and every 10 minutes afterwards,\nwhether IPv4 and IPv6 have a route. Remove a network without one from\ng_reachable_nets to avoid futile outbound connection attempts, and add\nit back once a route appears.\n\nThe first check is delayed to not react to short gaps at boot, which\nwould drop anchors and fixed seeds of that network for the entire run.\nA network is only marked unreachable if another network has a route,\nsince otherwise we are probably just offline.\n\nThe check only runs if automatic outbound connections are made, -onlynet\nis not used (which serves as opt-out), and the network is not reached\nvia a proxy.",
      "committer": {
